\section{Granularity and scope}{

One record per register \strong{document} (\code{document_id = "eib_<id>"}); one
project has many documents sharing \code{project_number}. ALL document types the
register holds for the country are kept, with the native type label in
\code{role} / \code{native_type} and one \verb{attachment_urls_<type-slug>} section each.
The types are not reclassified. Labels such as \code{ESIA}, \verb{Environmental Impact Assessment} and \code{SEA} identify full reports (although the \code{ESIA} bucket also
holds permits, decisions and placeholder rows); \code{ESDS}, \code{ESCS} and \code{NTS} are
summaries. A \verb{Link to promoter website} row may have no file: the record \code{url}
is the register page, and the download of its (non-existent) file is recorded
as a failure in \code{download_status}. Coverage is EIB-financed projects only
(publication from about 2011), not national completeness.
}

\section{Geography}{

The register tags documents with ISO-2 country codes (plus non-ISO tags such
as \code{C7} "EU Countries" and regional \code{A1}-\code{A9}). A record matches when ANY of
its tags equals the requested code (multi-country records appear under each
requested country with the same \code{document_id}). Regional/non-ISO-only and
untagged rows are excluded. The complete native tag list is kept in
\code{country_codes} / \code{country_labels}.
}

\section{Listing and completeness}{

One request to \verb{/provider-eib-plr/app/registers/list?countries=<ISO2>}
returns the whole filtered list. When the response's \code{totalItems} differs
from the returned row count a \code{planscanR_warning_partial} states both
numbers (the register itself shows such gaps). Per-record metadata comes
from \verb{/registers/item/\{id\}}; files from \verb{/attachments/registers/\{id\}.pdf}.
Files over \code{max_file_size_mb} are not silently dropped: they stay in the
record and get \code{skipped_size} in \code{download_status}.
